James wanted to create a long scrolling webpage with dynamic elements revealed through scrolling and inquired about this design's terminology and Dreamweaver templates. I explained that this style is termed a "parallax" or "scrolling effect" page. I suggested searching for parallax templates online from sources like ThemeForest and integrating JavaScript libraries such as Jarallax or ScrollMagic for animations. I also recommended customizing templates with CSS, ensuring responsive design, and utilizing Dreamweaver's features for live editing. Lastly, I emphasized testing across devices and browsers to ensure optimal performance.
